      "text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 20 #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Enhanced Southwest Monsoon (Habagat)\nIssued at: 5:00 AM, 24 September 2025(Wednesday)\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Zambales and Bataan.\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: Possible FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, expect light to moderate rains over Cavite, Bulacan, Metro Manila, Rizal, Laguna and Nueva Ecija within the next 3 hours.\nLight to moderate rains affecting Tarlac(San Jose, Concepcion, Bamban, Capas), Pampanga(Mabalacat, Mexico, Santo Tomas, Porac, Angeles, Santa Rita, Minalin, Bacolor, San Fernando, Floridablanca, Macabebe, Masantol, Guagua, Sasmuan, Lubao, Apalit, San Simon), Batangas(San Nicolas, Agoncillo, Taal, Bauan, Mabini, San Luis, Santa Teresita, Alitagtag, Cuenca, San Jose, San Pascual, Lipa, Ibaan, Batangas City, Lemery, Laurel, Tanauan, Talisay, Santo Tomas, Malvar, Balete, Mataasnakahoy, Tingloy, Padre Garcia, Rosario, Taysan, Lobo, Calaca) and Quezon(Pagbilao, Padre Burgos) which may persist within 3 hours and may affect nearby areas.\n\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 8:00 AM today.\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
